            <ArticleTitle>Severe congestive lupus cardiomyopathy complicated by an intracavitary thrombus: a clinical and echocardiographic followup.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1278-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Severe congestive cardiomyopathy is an uncommon complication of systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE). We describe a patient with active SLE and a circulating anticoagulant. She presented with a rapidly progressive cardiomyopathy, complicated by an intracavitary thrombus and cerebral infarction. The course of the disease is described, with special emphasis on the usefulness of consecutive echocardiographic studies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
